      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The card reads,</p>\n<blockquote>Whenever The Scholar would be dealt Damage, reduce that Damage to 0.\"\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nSo since it doesn't say \"immune to damage,\" does this mean that irreducible damage will still get through normally? Hasn't come up in any of my games yet (thus far, the only time we've used him is against the Ennead, where this card and an out of turn Alchemical Redirection bought us a round of safety), but I want to make sure for future games.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If damage is \"irreducible\", than how could expect the worse \"reduce\" the damage to 0? Irreducible trumps reduction effects.</p>",
